<title>POLAND: NFI UNITS DOWN IN WARSAW CONTINUOUS TRADE.</title>
<headline>NFI UNITS DOWN IN WARSAW CONTINUOUS TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mass privatisation units closed 1.7 percent lower, at 88 zlotys, in higher turnover in Warsaw bourse continuous trade on Monday.</p>
<p>The five stocks in the continuous system -- BIG, BPH, Debica, Rolimpex and Eledtrim -- did not trade.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
